From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:07:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(nethernet): close Bedrock sessions when the connection
 drops

NetherNet 2.0.0.CR4-20261001 leaves a client channel open when its peer connection fails after the handshake. It retries failed peer connections only during the handshake and otherwise ignores RTC_FAILED. ViaProxy then keeps the Java player connected to a backend that can no longer send or receive, until the Java client's keepalive times out about 30 seconds later.

NetherNet closes such channels since 2026-10-18 and fires a TransportDisconnectReason first, CONNECTION_LOST for a failed ICE path. Use 2.0.0.CR6-20261030.131938-23, the build the ViaFabricPlus Bedrock add-on already ships. It depends on the libdatachannel 0.24.6.0-20261029 bundle this build already pins.

diff --git a/build.gradle b/build.gradle
index 86a6475b419a2bb901602fd2588c152bf21bfca1..600235a2b1588415242d4fad5bb360225d7a4072 100644
--- a/build.gradle
+++ b/build.gradle
@@ -124,7 +124,7 @@ dependencies {
     includeInJar("net.raphimc:MinecraftAuth:5.0.3-20260923.192703-2") {
         exclude group: "com.google.code.gson", module: "gson"
     }
-    includeInJar("org.cloudburstmc.netty:netty-transport-nethernet:2.0.0.CR4-20261001.235918-13") {
+    includeInJar("org.cloudburstmc.netty:netty-transport-nethernet:2.0.0.CR6-20261030.131938-23") {
         exclude group: "io.netty"
         exclude group: "org.bouncycastle"
         exclude group: "dev.opencollab", module: "libdatachannel-java"
